{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 10, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-atg", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Antigua and Barbuda (ATG) from a pure blueprint-only stub, same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8. Delivered: marketentry.facts (investigated and ruled OUT a plausible-sounding but wrong candidate -- the Antigua and Barbuda Bureau of Standards administers an unrelated product-standards Act, not procurement -- confirming instead the Procurement Board + Procurement Unit created by the Procurement Administration Act 2011 (No. 16 of 2011), operating today at tendersboard.gov.ag under its pre-2011 brand name even though the Act legally renamed it, handled by citing the Act's legal names as owner-authority while citing the real operating domain as provenance rather than picking one and dropping the other; a real, current, tiered vendor-registration system (Class 1/2/3 at EC$50,000/EC$1,000,000 breakpoints) grounding a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE for this family -- a discrete 3-tier threshold recompute, distinct from Bulgaria's %-formula, Albania's flat constant, and Azerbaijan/Armenia's boolean reads; business registration investigated as a TWO-ACT model (ABIPCO company registration, then a separate IRD taxpayer-ID application), structurally like Japan's, unlike ALB/ARM/AZE's one-act models) + statute.facts (Companies Act 1995, Labour Code, Data Protection Act 2013) + honest scope-narrowing (rep-spec-basis nil for ATG -- the Act's suspend/debar power delegates its actual grounds to Regulations this iteration could not locate/verify as gazetted, so it was not modeled, mirroring Albania's disciplined omission of its own similar list-power).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session: (1) spot-checked citation URLs live via curl (WebFetch itself failed with an incomplete-TLS-chain error on every *.gov.ag host, same class of environment l