{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 13, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1512", :event/action "Added Mexico (:MEX) as a 4th jurisdiction to luggage.facts/catalog (was USA/ITA/CAN), the last of the iteration-6 pre-screened candidates except isic-1430 (knitwear). Citations: NOM-020-SCFI-1997 (leather/hide labeling requirement for luggage and leather goods, HIGH confidence) + Ley Federal del Trabajo (federal labor-standards compliance, HIGH confidence). Deliberately did NOT add a CITES/exotic-skin-sourcing requirement analogous to USA/ITA's, despite Mexico being a CITES party via SEMARNAT -- that angle was not researched/verified this iteration, so it was honestly left out rather than asserted from general knowledge.", :event/verification "Citations independently verified before writing: NOM-020-SCFI-1997 confirmed directly on PROFECO's official NOM listing (profeco.gob.mx/juridico/normas/noms_economia.asp), matching exact scope text and in-force date (1998 publication, 1999-04-27 effective). Ley Federal del Trabajo confirmed by direct primary-text read -- first attempt (diputados.gob.mx direct PDF link) failed with a connection error, second attempt succeeded via the official gob.mx mirror (gob.mx/cms/uploads/attachment/file/156203/1044_Ley_Federal_del_Trabajo.pdf, HTTP 200, 1.7MB, 236 pages), pdftotext-confirmed genuine content ('LEY FEDERAL DEL TRABAJO / CAMARA DE DIPUTADOS DEL H. CONGRESO DE LA UNION ... publicada ... el 1o de abril de 1970'). clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 34 tests / 112 assertions, 0 failures both times. Also discovered and preserved (rather than discarded) a stray, already-superseded detached-HEAD commit left in the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1512 checkout by an unrelated concurrent session (a deps.edn :local/root retarget) -- confirmed via diff that its content was byte-identical to, and fully contained in, origin/main's own equivalent commit before treating it as safely supersedable; pointed a local branch (preserve/stray-detached-bce0813) at it rather than letting it become unreachable. Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-1512-mex-luggage-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1512/merges, commit 3c47c1708fad3090e48451ecf6f827b29f29d5cc) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 9d6b8a95a601 -> 3c47c1708fad (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (target was pre-screened in iteration 6's classification pass).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration -- kept pace on the cheaper real-world-ingest-gap axis. After isic-1512, only isic-1430 (knitwear) remains from iteration 6's pre-screened candidate list -- once that lands, a future iteration must run a fresh :spec-basis classification pass over the isic 'none-measured' bucket or extend the method to isco/assoc/municipality/cofog/unspsc, since the original candidate list will be exhausted. Axis alternation is now 6 prod-ready / 7 real-world-ingest-gap across 13 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 13, :event/at "2026-07-21T14:25:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 14, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-and", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Andorra (AND) from a src/marketentry-and-src/statute-absent stub (a pre-existing src/culture domain from an unrelated prior Wave-1 initiative was left untouched), same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10/12. Delegated to a fresh background agent (isolated standalone clone, not the shared checkout) with an explicit research+verify+scaffold+push-to-branch-only mandate. Delivered: marketentry.facts (investigated, rather than assumed, whether Andorra splits procurement regulation from e-procurement portal operation the way Benin's ARMP/DNCMP split does -- found NO split: Llei 14/2022 Art. 126/127/129 house the regulatory board, the official bidders' registry, AND the live e-procurement platform all within the same ministry, a genuinely different institutional shape; a REAL, populated rep-spec-basis for the first time in this family's history -- Art. 13.1.a)/13.1.f) directly extend procurement-exclusion grounds to a bidder's own representatives/administrators/significant shareholders, unlike Benin and Antigua and Barbuda which both deliberately left this nil; a two-act, two-authority business/tax registration model (company registry under one ministry, NRT tax-ID under a different one) closer in shape to Antigua and Barbuda's sequential model than Benin's single-guichet convergence, plus an honestly-disclosed THIRD layer -- a municipal/Govern commercial-activity authorization -- found but deliberately NOT modeled; the flagship check grounds on Art. 30.1's direct-contracting EUR thresholds, a newly-verified numeric-threshold shape) + statute.facts (Llei 20/2007 company law -- confirmed Andorra is NOT an OHADA-style supranational-company-law member, unlike Benin -- + Llei 31/2018 labor law, with a genuinely dated finding that the PREDECESSOR statute Llei 35/2008 was literally