{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 15, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1430", :event/action "Added Cambodia (:KHM) as a 4th jurisdiction to knitwear.facts/catalog (was VNM/BGD/USA) -- the LAST candidate from iteration 6's original pre-screened classification pass, closing out that queue entirely. Citations: Labor Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia (Kram dated March 13, 1997) Article 17 (enterprise-opening declaration to the Ministry in Charge of Labor, grounding plant-registration) and Article 137 (8hr/day, 48hr/week normal working-hours limit, grounding labor-standards), both HIGH confidence -- read directly from the primary law text; plus the Law on Standards of Cambodia (Royal Kram No. NS/RKM/0607/013, 24 June 2007), establishing the Institute of Standards of Cambodia under the Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy, grounding quality-standards, HIGH confidence.", :event/verification "Citations independently verified before writing: Labor Law Article 17 and Article 137 confirmed verbatim against the ASEAN-hosted primary-text PDF mirror (pdftotext-extracted) and independently cross-checked against the Council for the Development of Cambodia's (cdc.gov.kh, a government body) own plain-HTML summary page, which quoted Article 17 near-verbatim. Law on Standards of Cambodia confirmed verbatim against a cdc.gov.kh-hosted government summary PDF (Royal Kram number, promulgation date, MIME housing, and ISC's establishment all matched). clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 31 tests / 112 assertions, 0 failures both times. Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-1430-khm-knitwear-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1430/merges, commit 6188f5b5b609e8ae1df7985cd1bb3aa292436ee5) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 74ce7799a7e2 -> 6188f5b5b609 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (target was pre-screened in iteration 6's classification pass).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration -- kept pace on the cheaper real-world-ingest-gap axis. This closes out iteration 6's original pre-screened candidate list entirely (isic-1410/1430/1512/3020 all landed across iterations 9/11/13/15). A future real-world-ingest-gap iteration must run a fresh :spec-basis classification pass over the isic 'none-measured' bucket (still 164 repos, unclassified by this method) or extend the classification method to isco/assoc/municipality/cofog/unspsc before the next ingest-gap batch can be picked without ad hoc re-discovery. Axis alternation is now 7 prod-ready / 8 real-world-ingest-gap across 15 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 15, :event/at "2026-07-21T16:05:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 16, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-bdi", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Burundi (BDI) from a src/marketentry-and-src/statute-absent stub (a pre-existing src/culture domain from an unrelated prior Wave-1 initiative was left untouched), same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10/12/14. Delegated to a fresh background agent (isolated standalone clone) with an explicit research+verify+scaffold+push-to-branch-only mandate. Delivered: marketentry.facts (investigated, rather than assumed, whether Burundi splits procurement regulation from e-procurement portal operation -- found a THIRD, RICHER institutional shape than Benin's two-body split or Andorra's no-split finding: the Code des Marchés Publics' own Art. 6 creates THREE procurement organs -- CGMP (passation, at each contracting authority), DNCMP (contrôle a priori/a posteriori), and ARMP (an independent régulation authority with a dispute-resolution committee and disciplinary commission) -- with no dedicated e-procurement portal-operator body found; rep-spec-basis deliberately left nil after specifically checking Art. 55's ineligibility grounds and finding them entity-level only, no personnel-extension clause; a genuinely new flagship-check shape -- a 20%-of-a-related-base-contract's-own-value ceiling (Art. 37 al.8 + Art. 40's continuation/complementary gré-à-gré grounds), distinct from every prior sibling's percentage-of-turnover/bid-evaluation-margin/flat-currency/boolean-registry shapes; a two-act business/tax registration model (RCS company registry + separate OBR tax-ID) like Benin's, but with a TIGHTER operational convergence -- Burundi's guichet-unique now bundles both numbers into a single issued 'Certificat d'immatriculation', tighter than Benin's GUFE which itemises them separately even within one application) + statute.facts (specifically investigated and found Burundi is NOT an OHADA member state -- confirmed directly against OHADA's own official member-state list, a genuinely different finding-direction than Benin's OHADA-member status -- so Burundi's company law is its own domestic statute, Loi n°1/09/2011, not a supranational Acte Uniforme; the Code du Travail citation is honestly rated MODERATE-HIGH rather than HIGH after 5 distinct hosting attempts all failed to retrieve the law's own article text, though the citation itself was corroborated by two independent official-tier sources; a genuinely new, dated finding -- Burundi enacted its first data-protection law, Loi n°1/03 du 10 mars 2026, barely 4 months before this research, verified by OCR-ing a scanned-image government PDF with no native text layer).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session (not merely re-reading the agent's report): (1) fresh standalone clone confirmed the diff touches exactly the 19 intended files and src/culture + test/culture are byte-identical to main (empty diff); (2) independently confirmed Burundi's absence from OHADA's official member-state list via WebFetch; independently re-fetched and pdftotext-verified the company-law citation (Loi n°1/09, 30 mai 2011, Article 1 text and 'Registre du Commerce et des Sociétés' references all matched verbatim) directly from investburundi.bi; independently re-fetched the procurement code via the same Wayback Machine mirror the agent used and confirmed Article 6's three-organs clause, Article 13's independent-authority language, and the Article 37/40 20%-threshold figures all appear verbatim in the primary text; for the labor-code citation, independently attempted two more hosting mirrors myself (both failed, corroborating rather than contradicting the agent's own MODERATE-HIGH rating) and confirmed via WebSearch that five independent sources (NATLEX, webapps.ilo.org, papyrus.ilo.org, droit-afrique.com, cosybu.bi) cite the identical law title/number/date; for the data-protection law, independently downloaded the scanned PDF myself, ran my own tesseract OCR pass (not reusing the agent's output) across all 32 pages, and confirmed both Article 1's full quoted text and Article 42's Chapitre-V institution-creation text verbatim; (3) independently reconstructed the `:local/root` relative-path layout and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 38 tests / 116 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; (4) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (5) confirmed origin/main was untouched by the agent before merging. Landed via server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-bdi/merges, commit 40653074caad9d1df2b7ce40db232051ed2a5900) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 5e6fea51a6a8 -> 40653074caad (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- iteration 6's original pre-screened candidate list closed out at iteration 15; the next real-world-ingest-gap iteration needs a fresh :spec-basis classification pass over the isic 'none-measured' bucket (164 repos) or an extension of the classification method to isco/assoc/municipality/cofog/unspsc before a target can be picked without ad hoc re-discovery. Axis alternation is now 8 prod-ready / 8 real-world-ingest-gap across 16 iterations, evenly balanced -- a natural checkpoint.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 16, :event/at "2026-07-21T17:10:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 17, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-5011", :event/action "Added Philippines (:PHL) as a 5th jurisdiction to ferry.facts/catalog (was JPN/USA/GBR/NOR). Citation: Republic Act No. 9295 (Domestic Shipping Development Act of 2004) and its Revised Implementing Rules and Regulations, which lists 'Passenger Ship Safety Certificate' among the required Ship Safety Certificates the Maritime Industry Authority (MARINA) issues -- HIGH confidence, read directly (pdftotext) from MARINA's own hosted PDF. IMPORTANT PROCESS FINDING this iteration: iteration 6's original pre-screened isic real-world-ingest-gap candidate list closed out at iteration 15, so this iteration needed a fresh classification pass. Queried the already-committed manifest/itonami-fleet-audit.edn directly (no need to re-run the full 1155-repo audit) and found 184 isic repos flagged :none-measured (no facts.cljc detected at all, a DIFFERENT population from iteration 6's 70-repo 'has-facts-file-but-scores-as-gap' bucket). Sampling ~14 of these 184 revealed the bucket is DOMINATED by a genuinely different, valid actor architecture -- an equipment/batch/shipment operations-coordination governor (the '*ops' naming family: knittingops/coalops/quarryops/foodretailops/restaurantops/postalops/etc, plus non-'*ops'-named siblings like forestry/logging/fishing) that has NO jurisdiction-compliance-citation concept at all, architecturally analogous to the already-excluded isco family -- force-fitting a facts.cljc into these would be wrong, not a fix. BUT one sampled repo, cloud-itonami-isic-5011 (ferry), turned out to be a FALSE NEGATIVE in the audit script: it already has a genuine, well-formed 4-jurisdiction ferry.facts/catalog (JPN/USA/GBR/NOR, real citations) that the audit script's has-facts-file? detection somehow missed -- this iteration picked it as the real target instead of blindly scaffolding a new catalog into an '*ops'-architecture repo. The audit script's detection bug itself was NOT investigated/fixed this iteration (out of scope for a single batch) -- flagged here for whoever next touches scripts/itonami-fleet-audit.cljs.", :event/verification "Citation independently verified before writing: fetched marina.gov.ph's own hosted 'Revised-IRR-of-RA-9295.pdf' directly (HTTP 200), pdftotext-confirmed the exact promulgation clause ('pursuant to Paragraph 17, Section 10 of RA No. 9295... Domestic Shipping Development Act of 2004') and the explicit 'Passenger Ship Safety Certificate' listing among required Ship Safety Certificates. (A supplementary technical document, MARINA's own PSSRR Part B, was independently found and read but NOT cited directly -- its cover page reads 'SUBJECT FOR FINAL REVIEW', so only the clean, clearly-in-force R-IRR of RA 9295 was used as the citation, an honest confidence discipline consistent with this loop's charter.) The Philippine Official Gazette's own RA 9295 page and the Hellenic/Greek government sites investigated as an alternative jurisdiction both returned HTTP 403 to curl/WebFetch and were abandoned in favor of the Philippines, whose sites were reachable. clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 46 tests / 274 assertions, 0 failures both times. Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-5011-phl-ferry-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5011/merges, commit 5d5cfa057bac37014d1762edd720498e6ebf11f9) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced d0776e77077f -> 5d5cfa057bac (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins; note the pin was ALSO 2 commits stale even before this iteration's own change, both gaps closed by this single pin advance) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "14 sampled repos from the isic :none-measured bucket (cloud-itonami-isic-0210/0220/0311/0510/0899/1313/1391/4721/5224/561/5811/2432/5310/5819) all confirmed to be the '*ops'/operations-coordination actor architecture (equipment scheduling, batch/QC/shipment verification) with no jurisdiction-citation concept -- NOT genuine real-world-ingest-gap targets, architecturally analogous to the already-excluded isco family. cloud-itonami-isic-5011 (ferry) was the one exception found and used instead.", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration. The isic :none-measured bucket (184 repos, minus the now-fixed isic-5011) has NOT been exhaustively classified -- only ~14 sampled -- so a future real-world-ingest-gap iteration should either continue sampling this bucket for more ferry-5011-style false negatives, or investigate/fix the has-facts-file? detection bug in scripts/itonami-fleet-audit.cljs directly (which would surface any other false negatives in one pass instead of continued sampling), or extend the classification method to isco/assoc/municipality/cofog/unspsc as previously suggested. Axis alternation is now 8 prod-ready / 9 real-world-ingest-gap across 17 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 17, :event/at "2026-07-21T17:50:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 18, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-bfa", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Burkina Faso (BFA) from a src/marketentry-and-src/statute-absent stub (a pre-existing src/culture domain from an unrelated prior Wave-1 initiative was left untouched), same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10/12/14/16. Delegated to a fresh background agent (isolated standalone clone) with an explicit research+verify+scaffold+push-to-branch-only mandate. Delivered: marketentry.facts (investigated, rather than assumed by analogy to prior siblings, whether the current procurement law is still Loi n°039-2016/AN -- found it is NOT, replaced by Loi n°005-2024/ALT du 20 avril 2024, promulgated by the Transition President; investigated the procurement-regulation/control/portal-operation split and found a genuinely different DRAFTING SHAPE than Burundi's law -- both establish the same tripartite gestion/contrôle/régulation separation, but Burkina Faso's law only directly names ONE of the three bodies (the régulation authority) in its own text, leaving the other two to implementing décrets, unlike Burundi's law which names all three directly; filled in the names -- ARCOP (régulation, PM-attached, NOT Presidency-attached like Benin's ARMP) and DGCMEF (contrôle, ministry-embedded); found ARCOP's OWN statutory missions include 'le maintien du système d'information' -- the OPPOSITE allocation from Benin's shape where the control body operates the portal; a REAL, populated rep-spec-basis (Burkina Faso's law extends procurement-exclusion grounds to a bidder's own natural-person representatives, unlike Benin's consortium/subcontractor-only scope); a flagship PME preference-margin check (Décret n°2024-1748 Art. 122, 5%) explicitly noted as DISCRETIONARY ('peut être accordée') rather than Benin's MANDATORY wording, an honest legal-strength distinction) + statute.facts (confirmed Burkina Faso IS an OHADA member via OHADA's own official site, so its company law is the SAME OHADA AUSCGIE Uniform Act Benin's is -- notably adopted in Ouagadougou, Burkina Faso's own capital; Code du Travail (Loi n°028-2008/AN); investigated and found Burkina Faso's early, widely-cited 2004 data-protection law (Loi n°010-2004/AN, one of West Africa's first) has been ABROGATED and replaced by Loi n°001-2021/AN, while the CIL regulator's name was preserved across the transition -- unlike Benin's CNIL-to-APDP rename).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session (not merely re-reading the agent's report): (1) fresh standalone clone confirmed the diff touches exactly the 16 intended files (deps.edn + 15 src/test files) and src/culture + test/culture are byte-identical to main (empty diff); (2) independently re-fetched and pdftotext-verified the two native-text citations myself -- Code du Travail Art. 1er (fonction-publique.gov.bf) and the 2021 data-protection law's Art. 82 abrogation clause + Art. 45 CIL-creation clause (academiedepolice.bf) both matched verbatim; independently confirmed the IFU/Code Général des Impôts Art. 635 citation verbatim (dgi.bf, including the exact amending-law parenthetical); independently confirmed Burkina Faso's OHADA membership via OHADA's own official site; for the harder OCR-based procurement citations, independently downloaded the scanned arcop.bf PDFs myself (confirmed 'KM_958'/Konica Minolta scanner metadata, no native text layer), fetched French tessdata fresh, and ran my own independent tesseract OCR pass (not reusing the agent's OCR output) -- confirmed the Loi n°005-2024/ALT abrogation clause ('abroge la loi n°039-2016/AN...') verbatim, confirmed the rep-spec-basis exclusion clause ('les personnes physiques qui ont pouvoir de les représenter...') verbatim on my own OCR'd page, and confirmed the Décret n°2024-1748 Art. 122 PME-preference clause ('marge de préférence de cinq pour cent (5%)... petites et moyennes entreprises burkinabè...') verbatim, though noting my own OCR pass could not cleanly disambiguate the article-number-to-body-text mapping on that two-column-layout page (a legitimate minor confidence caveat consistent with the agent's own MODERATE, not HIGH, rating for that specific citation); independently WebSearch-corroborated the ARCOP creation decree's attributions and 'maintien du système d'information' finding; (3) independently reconstructed the `:local/root` relative-path layout and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 37 tests / 116 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; (4) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (5) confirmed origin/main was untouched by the agent before merging. Landed via server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-bfa/merges, commit 11e1da3453d30b503e8e1600d94f3aa65f3a9c08) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 5aa4cf3a005c -> 11e1da3453d3 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration. The isic :none-measured bucket (184 repos, minus isic-5011 fixed in iteration 17) remains largely unclassified (only ~14 sampled so far) -- a future real-world-ingest-gap iteration should continue sampling for more ferry-5011-style audit false-negatives, or investigate/fix the has-facts-file? detection bug in scripts/itonami-fleet-audit.cljs directly. Axis alternation is now 9 prod-ready / 9 real-world-ingest-gap across 18 iterations, evenly balanced.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 18, :event/at "2026-07-21T18:55:00Z"}
